832	     * '<normalizedTelephone>|<email or empty>|<householdId or empty>'}. Two owners are
833	     * duplicates only when their whole identity keys are equal; because the telephone is
834	     * part of the key, members of the same household with different telephones produce
835	     * different keys and are both allowed.
836	     *
837	     * @param normalizedTelephone the E.164 telephone (may be {@code null})
